## Before you upgrade {% #before-upgrade %}

Because an upgrade cannot be reversed, prepare for it first:

- Check that your installed [extensions](/docs/products/databases/postgresql/extensions) support the target version.
- Take a [manual backup](/docs/products/databases/postgresql/backups#manual) right before you start.
- Run your test suite against a new database created on the target version.
- Make sure your application reconnects when its connections are closed.
- Read the migration notes in the [PostgreSQL release notes](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/) for each major version you move past.

## Changes in PostgreSQL 19 {% #postgresql-19 %}

The [PostgreSQL 19 release notes](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/19.0/) list every change. These are the ones most likely to affect application code:

- `json_array()` over a query that returns no rows now returns an empty JSON array instead of `NULL`.
- `standard_conforming_strings` can no longer be turned off, so backslashes in ordinary string literals are always literal characters. Use `E'...'` strings for escape sequences.
- A role that signs in with an MD5 password now gets a warning after each successful login. MD5 support will be removed in a future PostgreSQL release, so move those roles to SCRAM-SHA-256 passwords.

# Pause and resume {% #pause-resume %}

{% only_dark %}
![Database settings status card](/images/docs/products/databases/postgresql/dark/settings.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Database settings status card](/images/docs/products/databases/postgresql/settings.avif)
{% /only_light %}

A paused database stops its compute but keeps its storage, configuration, and credentials. Pause a database you are not using to stop paying for compute; resume it when you need it again. In the Console, open **Settings** > **General** and use the **Running** toggle in the Details card, then click **Update** to apply it. From the API, update the status:

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
import { Client, Postgresql } from 'node-appwrite';

const client = new Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>')
    .setKey('<YOUR_API_KEY>');

const postgresql = new Postgresql(client);

await postgresql.update({
    databaseId: '<DATABASE_ID>',
    status: 'paused',
});
```
```server-deno
import { Client, Postgresql } from "npm:node-appwrite";

const client = new Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>')
    .setKey('<YOUR_API_KEY>');

const postgresql = new Postgresql(client);

await postgresql.update({
    databaseId: '<DATABASE_ID>',
    status: 'paused',
});
```
